| !Run for !@NAME@ - built with the riscos-gtk devkit
| A UnixLib program converted to Absolute (AIF), statically linked with
| GTK 3: it needs SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport (PackMan).
| riscos-gtk-package fills in @NAME@, @PROGRAM@ and @SLOT@.
Set @NAME@$Dir <Obey$Dir>
IconSprites <@NAME@$Dir>.!Sprites
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 IfThere System:Modules.SharedULib Then RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error @NAME@ needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later. Install it with PackMan.
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 IfThere System:Modules.ARMEABISupport Then RMLoad System:Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 Error @NAME@ needs the ARMEABISupport module. Install it with PackMan.
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 IfThere System:Modules.PThrTicker Then RMLoad System:Modules.PThrTicker
RMEnsure PThreadTicker 0.01 RMLoad <@NAME@$Dir>.PThrTicker
| The Log and the font cache go in the scrap directory
CDir <Wimp$ScrapDir>.@NAME@
| fontconfig keeps its cache here (fonts/fonts.conf names it): make it
| now, as fontconfig may not manage to on RISC OS
CDir <Wimp$ScrapDir>.@NAME@.fontcache
| The WimpSlot holds the program; the C heap grows it as needed (no
| dynamic area, so no logical address space is reserved).
WimpSlot -min @SLOT@K -max @SLOT@K
| %*0: a file double-clicked in the Filer (riscos_gtk_app_init converts it)
Run <@NAME@$Dir>.@PROGRAM@ %*0
